						</ul>
																																																									<div id="authorBiographyModal1" uk-modal>
												<div class="uk-modal-dialog uk-modal-body">
													<button class="uk-modal-close-default" type="button" uk-close></button>
													<h2 class="uk-modal-title">Sabuj Saha</h2>
																											<p class="uk-text-meta"><span  uk-tooltip="title: Affiliation" uk-icon="icon: location"></span> Oklahoma State University, USA.</p>
																										<p class="uk-text-meta">
																											</p>
																											<p><p>Sabuj Saha is a finance enthusiast and loves to explore the impact of innovation and information in financial decision-making. After Completing BBA (2014) and MBA (2016) in Accounting &amp; Information Systems, University of Dhaka, Mr. Saha worked as a Business Analyst in a startup for 6 months. Later, he worked as a Financial Compliance Analyst in Beximco Pharmaceutical for 1.5 years. Then Mr. Saha did his dual masters from   Oklahoma State University, USA in 2022: MS in Quantitative Financial Economics and MS in Business Analyst &amp; Data Science. Currently, he has been preparing to apply for a PhD in Finance. His research interests are sustainable financing, information disclosure, and FinTech.</p></p>
																									</div>
											</div>
										
																										<div id="authorBiographyModal2" uk-modal>
												<div class="uk-modal-dialog uk-modal-body">
													<button class="uk-modal-close-default" type="button" uk-close></button>
													<h2 class="uk-modal-title">Ahmed Rizvan Hasan</h2>
																											<p class="uk-text-meta"><span  uk-tooltip="title: Affiliation" uk-icon="icon: location"></span> The Pennsylvania State University, USA.</p>
																										<p class="uk-text-meta">
																											</p>
																											<p><p>Ahmed Rizvan Hasan is an Assistant Professor of Accounting at the University of Dhaka, Bangladesh. Currently, he is pursuing a Master’s in Accounting Analytics at Pennsylvania State University. Rizvan has more than 7 years of experience in academia. Before joining the University of Dhaka, he used to work at Primeasia University, as Lecturer and Assistant Proctor. He completed his undergraduate and graduate degrees from the Department of Accounting &amp; Information Systems, University of Dhaka. His research interests include but are not limited to - Financial and Risk Reporting, Corporate Governance, Business Information Systems, and Accounting Analytics etc. He has worked on research projects funded by the University Grants Commission (UGC) of Bangladesh and Centennial Research Grant (CRG), University of Dhaka.</p></p>
																									</div>
											</div>
										
																										<div id="authorBiographyModal3" uk-modal>
												<div class="uk-modal-dialog uk-modal-body">
													<button class="uk-modal-close-default" type="button" uk-close></button>
													<h2 class="uk-modal-title">Alvi Mahmud</h2>
																											<p class="uk-text-meta"><span  uk-tooltip="title: Affiliation" uk-icon="icon: location"></span> Oklahoma State University, USA.</p>
																										<p class="uk-text-meta">
																											</p>
																											<p><p>Alvi Mahmud is a finance professional with adequate knowledge of data. He worked for the Central Bank of Bangladesh for 3 years before moving to the USA to complete his master's degree. He worked as a government contract support for a couple of years before joining the private sector as a financial analyst. Alvi is enthusiastic about fintech development and applying new data trends in the finance domain.</p></p>
																									</div>
											</div>
										
																										<div id="authorBiographyModal4" uk-modal>
												<div class="uk-modal-dialog uk-modal-body">
													<button class="uk-modal-close-default" type="button" uk-close></button>
													<h2 class="uk-modal-title">Nujhat Ahmed</h2>
																											<p class="uk-text-meta"><span  uk-tooltip="title: Affiliation" uk-icon="icon: location"></span> Oklahoma State University, USA.</p>
																										<p class="uk-text-meta">
																											</p>
																											<p><p>Nujhat Ahmed is currently a graduate student, pursuing MS in Quantitative Finance at Oklahoma State University. She was a banker by profession and worked as an Associate Manager at BRAC Bank Limited. Ms. Nujhat completed her BBA and MBA degrees in Accounting &amp; Information Systems from the University of Dhaka. She is an Endeavour Leadership Program (ELP) alumnus. Her research interests include Capital Structure, Risk Disclosure, FinTech, and Information Technology.</p></p>
																									</div>
											</div>
										
																										<div id="authorBiographyModal5" uk-modal>
												<div class="uk-modal-dialog uk-modal-body">
													<button class="uk-modal-close-default" type="button" uk-close></button>
													<h2 class="uk-modal-title">Nahida Parvin</h2>
																											<p class="uk-text-meta"><span  uk-tooltip="title: Affiliation" uk-icon="icon: location"></span> Oklahoma State University, USA.</p>
																										<p class="uk-text-meta">
																											</p>
																											<p><p>Nahida Parvin is an accounting and finance enthusiast with a passion for exploring the transformative impact of innovation and technology on various aspects of finance &amp; and accounting. Currently pursuing “Master's in Quantitative Finance” at Oklahoma State University, she holds a Master of Business Administration (2019) and a Bachelor of Business Administration (2017) in Accounting and information Systems from the University of Dhaka, Bangladesh. With a keen interest in academia, Nahida served as the "Lecturer of Accounting" and "Program Coordinator" at Universal College Bangladesh, a global partner of Monash College Australia, for 2.5 years. Her brief tenure as a "Lecturer of Accounting" at Ahsanullah University of Science &amp; Technology further enriches her academic experience. Nahida's research focus includes ESG accounting, Sustainable finance and accounting Fintech, and Circular Economy.</p></p>
																									</div>
											</div>
										
																										<div id="authorBiographyModal6" uk-modal>
												<div class="uk-modal-dialog uk-modal-body">
													<button class="uk-modal-close-default" type="button" uk-close></button>
													<h2 class="uk-modal-title">Hemal Karmakar</h2>
																											<p class="uk-text-meta"><span  uk-tooltip="title: Affiliation" uk-icon="icon: location"></span> Oklahoma State University, USA.</p>
																										<p class="uk-text-meta">
																											</p>
																											<p><p>Hemal Karmakar holds a Bachelor of Business Administration in Finance from the University of Dhaka, Bangladesh. After working as a Business Analyst for a Canada-based software firm, he is currently pursuing a Master's in Quantitative Finance at Oklahoma State University. Hemal plans to further his academic journey with a Ph.D. in Finance, focusing on Corporate Finance and Investment Management.</p></p>
																									</div>
											</div>
										
													
